---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import corrections from "../data/corrections.json";
---
<Base title="For Michael" eyebrow={corrections.count + " things the records say differently"}
      dek="Every place where a document and the family tree disagree, or where a document says something the tree does not say at all — with the source for each, so every line can be checked.">

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{corrections.count}</div><div class="l">corrections and additions</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">{corrections.documented}</div><div class="l">rest on a document that has been read</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">changed in the tree or the charts</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="prose">
      <p><strong>This page is addressed to the person who built the tree.</strong> An archive that
      only ever agrees with its source is not doing any work — so here is the list of places where
      this one disagrees, in the open, with the citation attached to every line.</p>
      <p><strong>Nothing here has been applied.</strong> The charts on this site draw Michael's
      export exactly as it was given, because it is his research and the corrections are proposals,
      not edits. Three of the twenty-seven are marked <em>candidate</em> or <em>flagged</em> rather
      than documented, which means the archive thinks it is probably right and is telling you it is
      not certain.</p>
      <p>The commonest single error is not a wrong name. <strong>It is a wrong year</strong> — and
      almost always a birth year, on a person the tree could not date from a document. Giovanni
      Arena is out by eleven years, Michele Donato by five, Salvatore Mazza by six. That pattern is
      worth knowing when you look at any other undated birth in the tree.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {corrections.groups.map((g) => (
    <section class="blk">
      <div class="lab">{g.kind}</div>
      <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:14px">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>The tree says</th><th>The record says</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {g.rows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{r.slug && r.slug !== "—"
                  ? <a href={u("/people/" + r.slug)}><strong>{r.who}</strong></a>
                  : <strong>{r.who}</strong>}
                  {r.confidence !== "documented" && <><br /><span class="small" style="color:var(--ink-3)">{r.confidence}</span></>}
                </td>
                <td class="small">{r.treeSays}</td>
                <td>{r.recordSays}</td>
                <td class="small">{r.source}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="blk" style="border-bottom:0">
    <h2>How to read the confidence</h2>
    <div class="rec" style="margin-top:16px">
      <div class="k">documented</div>
      <div class="v">A record has been read and it says this. You can open the citation and see it.</div>
      <div class="w">24</div>
      <div class="k">inferred</div>
      <div class="v">No record names this person, but one names someone travelling on the same day
      or the same ship, and the inference is short.</div><div class="w">1</div>
      <div class="k">candidate</div>
      <div class="v">The best match in an index, with something still not quite right about it —
      a spelling, an age. Probably correct. Not proved.</div><div class="w">1</div>
      <div class="k">flagged</div>
      <div class="v">A problem identified and deliberately <em>not</em> resolved, because resolving
      it would need a record nobody has read yet.</div><div class="w">1</div>
    </div>
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:22px">The full reasoning for each of these sits on the page it
    came from — <a href={u("/scilla")}>Scilla</a> for the Calabrian registers,
    <a href={u("/crossings")}>The Crossings</a> for the manifests,
    <a href={u("/nudgee")}>Nudgee</a> for the burials and
    <a href={u("/queensland")}>Queensland</a> for the BDM index. Where this archive has been
    <em>wrong</em>, that is on <a href={u("/method")}>Method</a>, which is the more useful page.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
